Description: No ads, downloads, privacy, and TikTok's own checks answered the way an
 unmodified phone would.
 .
 ▍NO ADS
 A feed item TikTok's own server marked as an ad never becomes an object at all — refused
 at the model itself, the moment it is built, rather than a view hidden after the fact.
 A separate splash-ad surface is suppressed too.
 .
 ▍DOWNLOAD
 One button, right beside like, comment and share, on the video actually on screen.
 Saved straight into Photos — no list to open, no second place to look.
 .
 ▍PRIVACY
 Three separate switches, not one — a story's seen mark, a message's read receipt and a
 profile view report to three different places, so turning one off never touches the
 other two. Never touches what this device's own screen shows.
 .
 ▍HIDES THE JAILBREAK
 TikTok asks many places whether the device is modified: a direct jailbreak check, its
 signing information, whether the app looks like a genuine App Store build, whether an
 embedded provisioning profile exists, and more. Each is answered the way it would be on
 an unmodified phone. Nothing here touches a purchase, a receipt or a subscription —
 deliberately, even where a reference tweak names a jailbreak check living inside that
 surface.
 .
 ▍SEE WHAT IT CAUGHT
 Hold two fingers anywhere in TikTok for a real settings screen: a switch and an
 explanation for every feature, and live numbers behind each hook. Arabic and English.
 .
 TESTED ON TikTok 46.4.0. Nothing is pinned to a version number: every class is looked up
 at runtime and skipped if it is not there.
 .
 Architecture was read from BandarHL's and al3raQe's published BHTikTok source
 (github.com/BandarHL/BHTikTok, github.com/al3raQe/BHTikTok) and from two further
 compiled references, NA9 For TikTok and VibeTok — none carry a LICENSE file, so all are
 read for where TikTok is hookable only, the same cautious way this project treats every
 unlicensed reference. No code is taken from any of them; every class named here was
 independently confirmed present in TikTok's own binary before being hooked.
 .
 Developed by Ibrahim Ismail AL-Rahn. Open source under the GNU GPL v3.
